commit f25c90f9
Sandbox test helpers /agentgear and /agentskill; agent body reads mission objects

For the bot squads on the test galaxy. Both helpers are off unless
Core3.AgentGear = true (test_galaxy.py --config AgentGear=true) and only work
for accounts in Core3.AgentAccounts, so they never act on live players.

/agentgear basic|boss|support: a weapon for the starting profession, bone or
composite armor, stimpacks for medics; "support" gives doctor enhancement
packs, scout camp kits and an instrument. Items go into free equipment slots,
the rest into the inventory; the answer lists equipped/inventory/failed.
/agentskill <box> ...: grants skill boxes with their prerequisites and no XP
(the call character creation uses), so a squad can test trained roles
(doctor, entertainer, ranger, certified weapons). Real trainers stay a
separate test.

Agent body: decode MissionObjectMessage3 baselines and deltas (a terminal
refresh rewrites existing objects): type, title, description, reward,
difficulty, start/end/waypoint, target. New commands "missions" and
"mission_accept" (MissionAcceptRequest 0xF9).

Tested on the test galaxy: gear equips and stores (16 bots), training grants
all five boss-crew roles with prerequisites. Mission decoding is not yet
tested end to end (no mission terminal found in central Mos Eisley).

