commit 220e0f39
Sandbox /leash: never re-place a follower out of range; naming the leader keeps it on

Found by the bot squads (Dorn group): when the navmesh path stops short of
the leader (he stood on raised ground), the "3 m behind" point was still
12.5 m away, so the follower was moved to the same spot every 8 s. If the
computed point is still beyond the 10 m stuck range, use the leader's own
spot instead. Re-test: follower ends 2.7 m from the leader, once.
"/leash <current leader>" now answers "Already leashed" instead of turning
the leash off; the menu entry and a bare /leash still toggle.

Agent body: label CommandQueueRemove errors as the server sends them (1
locomotion, 2 missing ability or not allowed, 3 invalid target, 5 state).
Code 2 was reported as "wrong posture/locomotion", which hid that a fresh
scout lacks /forage.

