commit 09a56205
Sandbox /leash: server-side follow assist for group members

The client's /follow steers in a straight line and never tells the server,
so followers get stuck on corners and doorways. While a leash is on, the
server checks every 2 s; when the follower is more than 10 m from the leader
and has not closed the gap for 3 checks, it moves them to a walkable point
3 m short of the leader along a navmesh path (cells and doorways included).
Otherwise it does nothing and the client's follow keeps steering.

Start/stop with /leash <name>, /leash (target), /leash off, or right-click a
group member: "Leash (follow assist)" / "Stop leash" (SERVER_MENU10). Group
members on the same planet only; skipped in combat, dead, incapacitated or
mounted; refuses buildings the follower may not enter; ends on leaving the
group, logging out, changing planet or drifting over 512 m apart.
Core3.LeashEnabled = false turns it off.

Tested on the test galaxy with two bots: refused when not grouped; outdoor
unstick lands 3.0 m behind the leader, once; leader walking 91 s into the
cantina pulls a stationary follower into the same cell; right-click on/off;
leaving the group ends it. Not tested: private-building refusal, mounts,
a real client running /follow.

